Episode: Receptor & Reason 2026-09-29 - what the stand-in actually preserves: Dementia Language Models encode cognitive impairment as a controllable direction in weight space (synthetic Iowa Gambling Task play identifies human MCI at ROC-AUC 0.722 vs 0.657 for a human-trained classifier, with causal patching showing nothing broken); PASCode scores 1.5M phenotype-associated cells across 6.3M PsychAD nuclei and finds depression within Alzheimer's is astrocyte-led with IL-18 up; a kynurenic acid polygenic score beats measured serum kynurenic acid for lithium response in 457 bipolar patients; 7T MRS finds no regional glutamate difference in antipsychotic-free first-episode psychosis but inter-regional correlations in 6 of 10 pairs; tirzepatide blocks nicotine place preference, reinstatement and accumbal dopamine; itraconazole plus lacosamide rescues FXTAS flies at a fourfold lower dose; two THIK1 cryo-EM structures share a site and scaffold yet diverge at the C-terminal gate (CVN293 84.8% to 71.2% on deletion, C101248 enhanced); state-specific FEP over 78 ligand-channel pairs predicts efficacy not affinity, resolving sub-kcal/mol gaps because systematic errors correlate ~0.94 between states; T-REX orchestrates in silico binder design 2.43-fold over tree search; MechBench separates phenomenal-law recovery (35.00%) from mechanism recovery (13.75%); AutoBCI's architecture gain is 0.29 points while its forecaster cuts error 38.1%; and a 77-language ambient-scribe audit finds 3.4% serious note errors alone but 24% end-to-end, with amplification outrunning correction threefold
